  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Given that $P(A)=0.4,$ $P(B)=0.3,$ and $P(A\\cap B)=0.1,$ find $P({A}^{\u2032}\\cup B).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.4+0.3-0.1 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{\u2032}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/e3fecd795207853d1a17a3e23c0d2872a59fde1c0561b8e357aae4a1705ca651.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{\u2032}\\cup B)=0.1+0.2+0.4=0.7.\n$$",
